ReCLamO-Harness is a clean-room implementation that follows their design. No files
from either project are copied into this repository. Should any snippet ever be ported
verbatim, it keeps the upstream copyright line and MIT permission notice alongside it.

One module does carry verbatim text: src/reclamo/upstream.py holds the system prompt,
per-turn prompts and output layout of alexzhang13/rlm at tag v1.0.0 (commit 18a9368),
with the Qwen3-8B edits from the RLM paper (arXiv 2512.24601, App. C.1), so that the
authors' released mit-oasys/rlm-qwen3-8b-v0.1 checkpoint (MIT) can be used as the
planner. Those strings keep the copyright line of that tag's LICENSE,
"Copyright (c) 2025 Alex Zhang", and the MIT permission notice beside them.
